From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Baker <ConnorBaker01@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:40:19 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] libstore: tell an external builder whether Nix would build
 locally

Carried for Tribuchet. An external builder may decline a build by
exiting with status 222, and Nix then builds the derivation itself if
it can: the platform is this system's (or an extra platform, or the
derivation is builtin), the store has every required system feature,
and max-jobs is nonzero. Tribuchet must only decline a build that Nix
will then build, but its attach shim could only approximate that test
from `nix config show`, which cannot see a trusted client's settings
for one daemon connection.

Compute the test once per local build, in a single function, and use
that one value both for the fallback after a decline and for a new
`canBuildLocally` boolean in build.json, so the two cannot disagree.
The settings it reads are the ones the decline fallback already read;
in a daemon they include the client's settings for that connection,
because each connection runs in its own worker process.

An external build takes a local build slot, so with max-jobs 0 the
external builder never runs at all; the new test pins that down too.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5)
